8.3 Power Analysis and Non-Inferiority Fallback

Given meta-analytic effect sizes near zero for SAR, the original $N = 192$ assuming $d = 0.5$ is optimistic. Revised for $d = 0.3$: $N \approx 352$ per arm, inflated to 470 per arm for 25% attrition.

However, the assumption of $d = 0.3$ for $\text{API}_{\text{cap}}$ trajectory change is not empirically grounded. If the true effect is $d = 0.1$, $N \approx 3{,}142$ per arm.

Non-inferiority fallback: If no cohort data (ELSA, SHARE) supports $d \geq 0.2$, redesign the definitive RCT as a non-inferiority trial against standard care, with superiority as a secondary endpoint. Pre-register an MCID (minimum clinically important difference) at 10% slowing of decline.

Adaptive interim analysis with O'Brien–Fleming boundaries ($\alpha_1 = 0.005$, $\alpha_2 = 0.014$, $\alpha_3 = 0.045$) preserves overall type I error at 0.05. Futility stopping: conditional power < 0.20.

