Chapter 9: Closed-Loop Architecture

9.1 Feedback Structure with Delays

\text{Human} \to \text{Sensing} \to \text{Estimation} \to \text{Trajectory} \to \text{Detection} \to \text{Selection} \to \text{Robot} \to \text{Human}

Modeled as $\mathbf{X}_{t+1} = \mathbf{F}(\mathbf{X}_t, \mathbf{O}_{t-\tau_s}, I_{t-\tau_a}, \mathbf{E}_t, \mathbf{M}_t)$, where $\tau_s$ is sensing delay and $\tau_a$ is actuation delay.

9.2 Three-Level Architecture with Latency Budget Breakdown

Level Function Latency Budget Processing Location
Edge Sensing, safety QP, actuator command < 100 ms total On-robot
Host State estimation, trajectory analysis, policy computation 1–5 s Local server
Cloud Long-horizon modeling, archetype learning, model updates Asynchronous Cloud

Edge latency breakdown:

Pipeline Stage Latency
Sensor acquisition 10–50 ms
Feature extraction 5–20 ms
Partial belief update 10–50 ms
QP solve < 1 ms
Actuator command 5–10 ms
Total 30–130 ms

If the total exceeds 100 ms, $\Delta t_{\text{edge}}$ is increased to 20–50 ms and Lemma 2 is re-derived. The safety guarantee is conditional on meeting the latency budget.

9.3 Privacy-by-Design

Raw video/audio never leaves the Edge. Only embeddings/features are transmitted to Host, per GDPR data minimization. Granular consent is obtained per sensor modality.

9.4 Human-in-the-Loop Authority and Dynamic Consent

The preference state evolves as $\mathbf{H}_{t+1} = \mathbf{G}(\mathbf{H}_t, \mathbf{X}_t, \text{interaction history})$, and the intervention policy is $I_t = \pi(\hat{\mathbf{X}}_t, \Delta\hat{\mathbf{X}}_t, \mathbf{R}_t, \mathbf{S}_t, \mathbf{H}_t)$.

Dynamic consent ledger: Every increase in $\text{RobotAuthority}$ requires explicit confirmation. The constraint $\text{RobotAuthority} \leq \text{HumanDelegatedAuthority}$ holds except in pre-negotiated emergency protocols.

Emergency protocol governance:

· Tier 1 (Immediate physical safety): Robot acts autonomously, logs, notifies.
· Tier 2 (Medical emergency): Alerts emergency services, may administer pre-authorized intervention.
· Tier 3 (Behavioral emergency): Alerts only; no autonomous physical intervention.

Each tier has explicit triggers, pre-authorized actions, revocation protocol, and post-hoc review requirement. Protocols are negotiated during onboarding and reviewed every 6 months.

