Appendix F — RC-POMDP Solution Methods

F.1 The C-POMDP BPO Violation

Bellman's principle of optimality does not generally hold for C-POMDPs. Optimal C-POMDP policies may violate BPO and require randomization (Ho et al., 2024).

F.2 Correct Formulation: RC-POMDP

Use RC-POMDP: $\max_\pi V_R^\pi(b_0)$ subject to $V_C^\pi(b_t) \le \hat{c}(b_t)$ for all $b_t \in \text{Reach}^\pi(b_0)$. Then:

· BPO holds.
· Deterministic optimal policy exists.

The Lagrangian $L(\pi, \boldsymbol{\mu}) = V_R^\pi + \boldsymbol{\mu}^\top(\hat{c} - V_C^\pi)$ has zero duality gap under the Slater condition if cost constraints are strictly feasible, but the primal optimum may still require history-dependent constraint tightening.

F.3 PBVI for RC-POMDP with Density Error Bound

Backup $\alpha^{a,o}$ as standard, but prune $\alpha$-vectors violating the admissible cost bound. Error bound (Pineau et al., 2006): for belief set $\mathcal{B}$,

\|V_t^{\mathcal{B}} - V_t^*\|_\infty \le \frac{R_{\max}}{1-\gamma} \cdot \epsilon_{\mathcal{B}},

where $\epsilon_{\mathcal{B}}$ is the density of $\mathcal{B}$ covering the reachable simplex $\bar{\Delta}$. This gives convergence as $\mathcal{B}$ becomes dense.

F.4 Policy Gradient with Constraints

For continuous action spaces, parameterize $\pi_\theta$ and optimize

\mathcal{L}(\theta, \boldsymbol{\mu}) = \mathbb{E}_{\pi_\theta}\left[\sum_t \gamma^t R(b_t, I_t)\right] - \sum_i \mu_i \left(\mathbb{E}_{\pi_\theta}\left[\sum_t \gamma^t c_i(b_t, I_t)\right] - d_i\right).

Update rules:

\theta \leftarrow \theta + \alpha_\theta \nabla_\theta \mathcal{L}, \quad \mu_i \leftarrow \max(0, \mu_i + \alpha_\mu(\mathbb{E}[C_i] - d_i)).

F.5 MCTS for Large RC-POMDPs

For large RC-POMDPs, we adopt Monte-Carlo Tree Search (CC-POMCP) for online planning, addressing the curse of history in lifelong care planning.

