Appendix G — QP Details and Complexity

G.1 Analytical Solution

The Edge QP is

\min_{I, \xi} \frac{1}{2} \|I - I^{\text{des}}\|_{\mathbf{R}}^2 + \frac{1}{2} w_{\text{slack}} \xi^2 \quad \text{s.t. } AI + b \le \xi, \; \xi \ge 0,

with $A = -L_g h(\boldsymbol{\mu}_t) \in \mathbb{R}^{1 \times m}$, $b = L_f h + \gamma_{\text{cbf}} \bar{h}_{\text{edge}} \in \mathbb{R}$.

KKT conditions:

\mathbf{R}(I - I^{\text{des}}) + \mu A^\top = 0, \quad w_{\text{slack}} \xi - \mu - \nu = 0, \quad \mu(AI + b - \xi) = 0, \quad \nu \xi = 0.

Case 1: $AI^{\text{des}} + b \le 0$. Then $\xi^* = 0$, $I^* = I^{\text{des}}$.

Case 2: $AI^{\text{des}} + b > 0$, $\xi^* > 0$. Then $\nu = 0$, $\xi^* = \mu/w_{\text{slack}}$, and

\mu^* = \frac{AI^{\text{des}} + b}{A \mathbf{R}^{-1} A^\top + 1/w_{\text{slack}}}, \quad I^* = I^{\text{des}} - \mu^* \mathbf{R}^{-1} A^\top.

G.2 Complexity

Precompute $\mathbf{R}^{-1}$ once (offline, $O(m^3)$). Per QP solve: $O(nm + m^2)$. For $n = 6$, $m = 4$, this is $O(40)$ flops — within the 10 ms Edge budget.

G.3 Edge Latency Budget Breakdown

Pipeline Stage Latency Notes
Sensor acquisition 10–50 ms Depends on sensor suite
Feature extraction 5–20 ms Motion, speech, activity
Partial belief update 10–50 ms If Edge does local propagation
QP solve < 1 ms Analytic solution
Actuator command 5–10 ms Motor control interface
Total 30–130 ms May exceed 100 ms budget

If the total exceeds 100 ms, $\Delta t_{\text{edge}}$ is increased to 20–50 ms, and Lemma 2 is re-derived with the larger $T_{\text{host}}$ accordingly. The safety guarantee is conditional on meeting the latency budget.

