Each agent $i$: $\mathbf{W}_i = \mathbf{W}_{\text{arch}} + \boldsymbol{\Delta}_i$, $\boldsymbol{\Delta}_i \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma_W^2 I)$.

H.2 Observation Noise

$\boldsymbol{\eta}_t \sim t_\nu(0, \Sigma_t^{\text{obs}})$ with $\nu = 5$. Sensor dropouts: $\text{Bernoulli}(0.15)$, imputed with previous value plus inflated noise.

H.3 Falsification Criteria

Metric Threshold Interpretation
Estimation RMSE (state) $\le \text{MDC}_{95}/2$ State estimation informative
Detection AUC (decline) $\ge 0.80$ Decline detection discriminative
Policy regret ratio $\le 0.15$ ARCS within 85% of oracle
Safety violation rate $\le \delta$ Safety constraint respected
Identifiability $\lambda_{\min}(\mathcal{I}(\mathbf{W}))$ $> 10^{-3}$ $\mathbf{W}$ estimable
Agency attribution FPR $\le 0.15$ Mis-attribution rate acceptable

The MDC-based derivation: the falsification thresholds are derived from the minimal detectable change ($\text{MDC}_{95}$) for each capability dimension. $\text{MDC}_{95} = 1.96 \sqrt{2} \cdot \text{SEM}$. The required estimation precision is $\text{MDC}_{95}/2$.

H.4 Adversarial Conditions

1. Sensor dropout: 30% channel dropout for 7 consecutive days.
2. Distribution shift: sudden change in hazard rate by factor 2.
3. Adversarial input: corrupted observations inducing false-positive decline detection.
4. Model misspecification: true coupling function $g(\cdot)$ is piecewise-linear while the estimator assumes $\tanh$.

For each condition, report degradation in each metric relative to nominal and test against pre-registered thresholds.

H.5 Agency Attribution Testing

The simulation must specifically test the $\alpha_t$ inference under ambiguous behavioral signals, with ground-truth $z_t$ known to the simulator. False-positive rate for attributing incapacity to deliberate choice (and vice versa) must be reported. Pre-registered threshold: FPR $\le 0.15$.

H.6 Multi-State Survival Functional Testing

Compare the multi-state formulation against the binary alternative. Report the frequency of perverse incentives (community-dwelling preservation at the cost of functional autonomy) under each. Pre-registered threshold: multi-state formulation reduces perverse-incentive frequency by $\ge 50\%$.

