Appendix I — Consent State Machine

Finite-state machine $\mathcal{C} = (Q, \Sigma, \delta_{\text{consent}}, q_0, F)$:

· States: $Q = \{q_{\text{granted}}, q_{\text{denied}}, q_{\text{withdrawn}}, q_{\text{emergency}}\}$.
· Alphabet: $\Sigma = \{\sigma_{\text{request}}, \sigma_{\text{approve}}, \sigma_{\text{deny}}, \sigma_{\text{withdraw}}, \sigma_{\text{emergency}}, \sigma_{\text{restore}}\}$.
· Transitions:

\delta_{\text{consent}}(q, \sigma) = \begin{cases} q_{\text{granted}} & \sigma = \sigma_{\text{approve}} \wedge q \in \{q_{\text{denied}}, q_{\text{withdrawn}}\} \\ q_{\text{denied}} & \sigma = \sigma_{\text{deny}} \\ q_{\text{withdrawn}} & \sigma = \sigma_{\text{withdraw}} \\ q_{\text{emergency}} & \sigma = \sigma_{\text{emergency}} \wedge \text{trigger valid} \\ q_{\text{granted}} & \sigma = \sigma_{\text{restore}} \wedge \text{clinician approval} \end{cases}

· Initial: $q_0 = q_{\text{denied}}$. Accepting: $F = \{q_{\text{granted}}, q_{\text{emergency}}\}$.

The policy $\pi$ is constrained to enforce $\text{Consent}_t = \text{True}$. Emergency overrides are logged, timestamped, and subject to post-hoc review within 48 hours.

