Appendix M — Belief Health Monitor and Recovery Protocol

M.1 Belief Health Metrics

Metric Definition Threshold
Effective sample size (particle filter) $\text{ESS} = 1 / \sum_i w_i^2$ $> 0.1 N$
Covariance conditioning $\kappa(\boldsymbol{\Sigma}_t) = \lambda_{\max} / \lambda_{\min}$ $< 10^6$
Prediction-observation discrepancy $\|\mathbf{O}_t - \mathbb{E}[\mathbf{O}_t \mid b_{t-1}]\|$ $< 3\sigma$

M.2 Recovery Protocol

If any metric crosses its pre-registered threshold:

1. Halt autonomous intervention.
2. Request human input (caregiver or clinician).
3. Re-initialize the belief from a safe prior (population archetype).
4. Log the event for post-hoc analysis.

M.3 Two-Tier Safety Switching

Tier 1 (nominal, Gaussian): Used when the belief distribution passes a multivariate normality test (Mardia skewness/kurtosis within pre-registered thresholds). Uses $\kappa_\delta^{\text{Gauss}} = \Phi^{-1}(1-\delta)$.

Tier 2 (robust, Cantelli): Used when normality is violated. Uses $\kappa_\delta^{\text{Cantelli}} = \sqrt{(1-\delta)/\delta}$.

Switching with hysteresis:

· Switch to Tier 2 when normality test fails at $p < 0.01$.
· Switch back to Tier 1 when normality test passes at $p > 0.05$ for 10 consecutive Host updates.

